{"name":"Warp & Weft","hex":"#e5d5c9","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state, quality, or condition of being twisted, physically or mentally.","A distortion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist or become twisted, physically or mentally.","To become twisted out of shape; to deform."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warp"},{"term":"weft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The horizontal threads that are interlaced through the warp in a woven fabric.","The yarn used for the weft; the fill."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of waif."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warp & Weft","blocks":[{"text":"Warp & Weft is the ninth studio album by American singer-songwriter Laura Veirs. Released on August 19, 2013, in the United States, and August 24, 2013, in Europe, the album was written by Veirs herself and produced by her husband Tucker Martine."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_%26_Weft"},{"title":"Warp and weft","blocks":[{"text":"In the manufacture of cloth, warp and weft are the two basic components in weaving to transform thread and yarn into textile fabrics. The vertical warp yarns are held stationary in tension on a loom (frame) while the horizontal weft is drawn through the warp thread. In the terminology of weaving, each warp thread is called a warp end; a pick is a single weft thread that crosses the warp thread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Warp_and_weft_2.jpg/330px-Warp_and_weft_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_and_weft"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png/250px-Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png/250px-Laura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaura_Veirs_-_Warp_%26_Weft.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Warp_and_weft_2.jpg/330px-Warp_and_weft_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Warp_and_weft_2.jpg/330px-Warp_and_weft_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warp and weft in plain weaving. See weaving for other weave pattens, such as twill.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWarp_and_weft_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Loom_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Loom_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Loom_%28PSF%29.png/1280px-Loom_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Loom_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Loom_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warped loom. Warp is wrapped onto the warp beam; as the cloth is made, the fell (woven part) is wrapped onto the breast beam next to the weaver.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoom_(PSF).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg/500px-Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg/1280px-Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg/500px-Raiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wrapping of the warp threads around the warp beam of a loom in preparation for weaving","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaiyani_muharramah-_Wanita_suku_badui_luar_DSCF2861.jpg"}],"sounds":{"warp":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/En-us-warp.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ae/En-us-warp.ogg/En-us-warp.ogg.mp3"}],"weft":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/En-us-weft.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/73/En-us-weft.ogg/En-us-weft.ogg.mp3"}]}}}